(6648181, 992158, 30214, '<td valign="top">haven''t looked at the set, so just came across your shot, Paul. Interestingly, it works much better in the context of the challenge by challenging it. Taken out of that context, it would not impress me much... photos of homeless and drunks juxtaposed with some happy street art or advertisements are dime a dozen :).</td>', 'haven''t looked at the set, so just came across your shot, Paul. Interestingly, it works much better in the context of the challenge by challenging it. Taken out of that context, it would not impress me much... photos of homeless and drunks juxtaposed with some happy street art or advertisements are dime a dozen :).', '2012-01-18 00:36:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6648184, 991990, 48769, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the votes. First submission, did not no what to expect. <br/>Thanks to the comments, I now see how much I was focused on lighting more then composition. It looks like two images, divided by that case divider. <br/>Well, it''s in the garbage now.<br/> <br/>Oh! here are the $1400.00 pictures.  :(<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=989772" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=989772</a> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=989773" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=989773</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-01-18 00:46:59.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the votes. First submission, did not no what to expect. Thanks to the comments, I now see how much I was focused on lighting more then composition. It looks like two images, divided by that case divider. Well, it''s in the garbage now. Oh! here are the $1400.00 pictures.  :(//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=989772 //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=989773', '2012-01-18 00:37:37.000000', '2012-01-18 00:46:59.000000', 0),
(6648187, 991199, 30364, '<td valign="top">Crap!  I gave you a middle of the road score for once.  I should have got my vote over on the distribution graph''s kerb, like your can.</td>', 'Crap!  I gave you a middle of the road score for once.  I should have got my vote over on the distribution graph''s kerb, like your can.', '2012-01-18 00:42:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6648189, 992158, 30364, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> haven''t looked at the set, so just came across your shot, Paul. Interestingly, it works much better in the context of the challenge by challenging it. Taken out of that context, it would not impress me much... photos of homeless and drunks juxtaposed with some happy street art or advertisements are dime a dozen :). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ha!  I thought much the same.  Cheers, Lev.</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: haven''t looked at the set, so just came across your shot, Paul. Interestingly, it works much better in the context of the challenge by challenging it. Taken out of that context, it would not impress me much... photos of homeless and drunks juxtaposed with some happy street art or advertisements are dime a dozen :).   Ha!  I thought much the same.  Cheers, Lev.', '2012-01-18 00:45:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6648190, 991990, 48769, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Purple_Girl:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m not totally sure what I''m looking at, I think it''s a melted lens and something else I can''t make out? Some interesting textures there, nice and crisp, I might have gone for colour to boost the interest a bit. A good shot overall, just not particularly eye-catching for me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I know..:( (head down) Thanks for the input, really appreciate it. :)<br/>I did not realize that you can''t see the photographers comment until after the voting. It''s hard to tell what it is without the comment.<br/>BTW, there was no color. Just burned gear...</td>', 'Originally posted by Purple_Girl: I''m not totally sure what I''m looking at, I think it''s a melted lens and something else I can''t make out? Some interesting textures there, nice and crisp, I might have gone for colour to boost the interest a bit. A good shot overall, just not particularly eye-catching for me.   I know..:( (head down) Thanks for the input, really appreciate it. :)I did not realize that you can''t see the photographers comment until after the voting. It''s hard to tell what it is without the comment.BTW, there was no color. Just burned gear...', '2012-01-18 00:45:31.000000', NULL, 0),
