(6648775, 991276, 124255, '<td valign="top">First off I gave this a 5 (although I remember almost giving it a 6). <br/> <br/>  I started one of the threads about my top three votes were probably DQ''s, I didn''t, and never do downgrade a photo because I think it might be breaking a rule. One of my top three choices got a ribbon so we will see, I may (and hope) have been wrong, if so I can''t wait to read what was done with the photograph because my understanding of the rules make "Basic" kind of boring to me. I hope it''s  a learning experience that will make me enter more photos. <br/> <br/>  I like your entry, wish I gave it the 6 because the effort and and time that I can see the setup took. Actually, I''d like to hear about how you captured the image. Nice job.<br/> <br/></td>', 'First off I gave this a 5 (although I remember almost giving it a 6).    I started one of the threads about my top three votes were probably DQ''s, I didn''t, and never do downgrade a photo because I think it might be breaking a rule. One of my top three choices got a ribbon so we will see, I may (and hope) have been wrong, if so I can''t wait to read what was done with the photograph because my understanding of the rules make "Basic" kind of boring to me. I hope it''s  a learning experience that will make me enter more photos.    I like your entry, wish I gave it the 6 because the effort and and time that I can see the setup took. Actually, I''d like to hear about how you captured the image. Nice job. ', '2012-01-18 15:20:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6648777, 992137, 113157, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 1m1A:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow, that''s so cool. Good patience in waiting for the right moment! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It wasn''t patience I set the camera set shoot 3 frames per second. Waited for the start of the explosions and held the shutter until the buffer was full.<br/> <br/>Here''s a link to the series: //www.pbase.com/mroper/down_with_old&amp;page=1 <br/> <br/>I guess you''ll have to cut and paste the link since it won''t work here.<br/>Thanks</td>', 'Originally posted by 1m1A: Wow, that''s so cool. Good patience in waiting for the right moment!  It wasn''t patience I set the camera set shoot 3 frames per second. Waited for the start of the explosions and held the shutter until the buffer was full. Here''s a link to the series: //www.pbase.com/mroper/down_with_old&page=1  I guess you''ll have to cut and paste the link since it won''t work here.Thanks', '2012-01-18 15:23:14.000000', NULL, 0),
